// Signing configuration (committed — safe to share)
//
// This is the base configuration the Xcode project points at. It deliberately
// contains no account-identifying values, so the repository can be public.
//
// To sign with your own Apple Developer account, create a file named
// `Config.xcconfig` next to this one:
//
//     echo 'DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID' > Config.xcconfig
//
// `Config.xcconfig` is gitignored and is picked up automatically by the
// optional include at the bottom of this file. If you don't create it, the
// build still works: Xcode falls back to "Sign to Run Locally", which is
// sufficient for running the app on your own machine.
//
// Find your Team ID at https://developer.apple.com/account (Membership
// Details), or in Xcode under Settings → Accounts.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// Optional local override. The `?` means a missing file is silently ignored,
// so cloning and building this repo requires no setup.
#include? "Config.xcconfig"
